# Code style consistency by directory tree

Top-level trees: **`ui/`**, **`base/`**, **`skia/`**, **`app/`**, **`content/`**, **`gis/`**, **`render/`**, **`testing/`**, **`build/`**, **`third_party/`**. Within each tree, match siblings. Align `gis/` / `render/` layout with smartgis (`gis/map`, `render/rhi/flycube`).

## Do

- When editing a file, read nearby code and match naming, include order, abstraction, and `BUILD.gn` patterns.
- Follow narrower rules first (`cxx-standard.mdc`, `naming.mdc`, `ui-views-skia.mdc`).

## Don’t

- Don’t import smartgis `core/` / C++23 idioms into `ui/views`.
- Don’t restyle `skia/` or `third_party/` to match a product edit.
